    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d8ec647_89a9b419",
        "filename": "scripts/dawn_features.gni",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-18T17:58:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe it\u0027s overly cautious but I don\u0027t want the build to break just because we\u0027re using a system clang that has slightly different behavior for an obscure warning. I think the `-Wall -Wextra` analyses can be considered stable but not everything else.\n\nAlso we don\u0027t want to get \"error: unknown warning option\" if we pass a `-Wno-*` that an older compiler doesn\u0027t understand.\n\nI guess if Tint has been doing it then it\u0027s fine, but seems like we may as well just do the theoretically safer thing.",
      "parentUuid": "7e3ae4ee_48e62101",
      "revId": "438e7533b7e7cbeeb41a9c095bfd38357190cf00",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
